    The one thing in Family that has to be XML. The client reads its key bindings out of a
    file with this shape before any addon Lua has run, so there is no Lua equivalent to
    write instead.

    **It is not listed in the .toc, and that is the point.** The client finds this file by
    its name in the addon's folder. Naming it in the .toc as well hands it to the ordinary
    UI XML loader, which knows Frame and Button and has never heard of Binding - and says
    so: "Unrecognized XML: Binding" on every login. Reported from play on Burning Crusade;
    Classic Era loads the same mistake without a word, which is why it shipped. WeakAuras
    does the same thing and lists no Bindings.xml either.

    What the Key Bindings window *calls* these is not here: it looks up the globals
    BINDING_HEADER_FAMILY and BINDING_NAME_FAMILY_TOGGLE, which Slash.lua sets from the
    locale table, so the words are translated like every other sentence Family says. A name
    written into this file would be English in every language and unreachable to the
    translators - which is the whole of the care this needed.

    Guarded, and not out of habit: a binding fires on a key press, which can happen while
    the player is still zoning in and before Family_UI has finished loading. An error thrown
    from here is thrown at whatever the player was doing.
-->
<Bindings>
    <Binding name="FAMILY_TOGGLE" header="FAMILY">
        if Family and Family.UI then Family.UI:Toggle() end
    </Binding>
</Bindings>
